%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% expect-output: true
% Scenario: a user path's outline through a matrix. The second form
% concatenates the matrix after the path is built and before the
% outline, then restores the CTM (PLRM3 §8.2 ustrokepath): the outline
% is twice as wide as the line width says, the CTM is unchanged
% afterwards (compared element by element, since the default CTM is
% the device's own), and page 2 gets the same outline from a doubled
% line width by hand.
15 setlinewidth 1 setlinecap
/before matrix currentmatrix def
{0 0 500 500 setbbox 120 150 moveto 360 220 lineto 220 500 lineto} [2 0 0 2 0 0] ustrokepath
/after matrix currentmatrix def
true 0 1 5 { dup before exch get exch after exch get eq and } for =
fill
showpage
30 setlinewidth 1 setlinecap
120 150 moveto 360 220 lineto 220 500 lineto strokepath fill
showpage
